# This Mac's arrangements of AeroSpace workspaces on its displays. setup_machine copies this file to
# ~/.config/dotfiles/arrangements once; `~/.config/aerospace/windows --apply <name>` applies one (see
# docs/aerospace.md, "Arrangements"), and `--check <file>` says what's wrong with a file (check_dotfiles runs it).
# A line for each workspace of an arrangement:
#   <name> <displays> <main|secondary> <workspace> <shape> <app>[, <app>…]
# displays: how many displays the arrangement is for, the same on all its lines; main or secondary: which of
# them the workspace goes on (System Settings → Displays → "Use as"); shape: tiles, rows, main, grid or
# accordion, as t in alt+w; the apps by the names AeroSpace gives them (aerospace list-apps), in the order the
# shape puts them. Every window of an app goes to its workspace; windows of apps not named stay where they are.
desk    2  main       1  tiles      Ghostty
desk    2  secondary  2  accordion  Slack
desk    2  secondary  7  tiles      Code
desk    2  secondary  8  tiles      Xcode, Simulator
desk    2  secondary  9  tiles      Android Studio, qemu-system-aarch64
laptop  1  main       1  accordion  Ghostty, Slack
